@startuml HostBrowserCDP
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: how an sbx agent drives a Chrome on the host over CDP — dedicated profile, dialled by IP, one allowed port
' covers: internal/hostdev/hostcdp.go
' covers: internal/hostdev/hostcdp_test.go
' covers: internal/run/choices.go (addonHostCDP, interfaceOptions, gateAddons)
' covers: internal/run/run.go (startHostCDP)
' covers: internal/run/outcome_test.go
' covers: internal/run/host_adb_test.go (TestEachHostAddOnFactNamesWhatTheRunLeftUp)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go (Spec allow)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/host_cdp.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/host_inference_test.go
' covers: packages/lib/proveo-host-cdp
' covers: packages/lib/agent-browser
' covers: e2e/host_chrome_test.go
' covers: defs/hermes/entrypoint.sh (PROVEO_HOST_CDP_PORT block)
' covers: defs/*/harness.manifest
'   the in-sandbox browser viewport ............ _spec/internal/sbx/browser-viewport.puml
'   the package it shares with adb ............. _spec/internal/sbx/host-android-adb.puml
'
' ── WHY (2026-09-27) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' The operator's hermes task is a logged-in site (Yahoo Fantasy): a login with 2FA
' the operator completes by hand, kept across runs, watched live. The sandbox has
' no display, and use_real_profile cannot decrypt a macOS Chrome profile (Keychain)
' from a Linux VM. A host Chrome on a DEDICATED profile gives all three.
'
' ── SHARED BY ALL DEFS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Every manifest declares capabilities.hostBrowser: cdp. The chrome add-on
' selects host Chrome. The browser add-on still selects in-sandbox Chromium.
' After the run accepts its choices, it starts or reuses host Chrome before
' image preflight or sandbox creation. --print opens no window.
' The Kit records the CDP port and allows localhost:<port>. After creation or
' reuse, the run checks that the guest has that port and upgrades the actual
' browser WebSocket. A kept sandbox must apply the selected Chrome setting.
' Fail before the agent launches if guest discovery or the handshake fails.
'
' proveo-host-cdp resolves the gateway in the guest. The application can dial
' the numeric address directly and keep sbx's normal proxy settings for other
' traffic. The wrapper supplies the discovered WebSocket in AGENT_BROWSER_CDP
' for agent-browser. Hermes uses the same gateway IP in BROWSER_CDP_URL.
' Neither client stores a run's endpoint in its persistent configuration.
' The lightweight agent-browser client lives in proveo/base. Codex gets its
' discovery skill at ~/.agents/skills. Hermes keeps its native browser client.
'
' Chrome DevTools MCP documents manual CDP attachment for sandboxed clients.
' https://github.com/ChromeDevTools/chrome-devtools-mcp/blob/main/docs/advanced-usage.md#connecting-to-a-running-chrome-instance
' Docker documents host-service policy as localhost:<port>.
' https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/workflows/development/#accessing-host-services-from-a-sandbox
' The 0.36.0 agent-browser wrapper listed a Chrome fixture tab from a separate
' Docker container with HTTP_PROXY and HTTPS_PROXY set to an unusable address.
' TestCodexUsesHostChromeFromSbx covers the same workflow on the sbx runtime.
'
' ── MEASURED FROM A GUEST (sbx v0.42.1, Chrome 153, host.docker.internal = 169.254.1.1) ─
'   via proxy  host.docker.internal:P/json/version   200, ws URL = ws://localhost:P/…  ✗ unusable in the VM
'   direct     host.docker.internal:P/json/version   "Host header is specified and is not an IP address or localhost"
'   direct     169.254.1.1:P/json/version            200, ws URL = ws://169.254.1.1:P/…  ✓
'   direct     ws://169.254.1.1:P/devtools/browser/…  101 Switching Protocols
' Chrome builds webSocketDebuggerUrl from the request's Host, and only accepts an
' IP or localhost there. So the entrypoint resolves host.docker.internal to its
' IPv4, sets BROWSER_CDP_URL=http://<ip>:<port>, and appends <ip> to NO_PROXY.
' Env only, never config.yaml: HERMES_HOME persists, and a stale browser.cdp_url
' costs every later run a 10 s discovery stall (hermes' own docstring).
' End to end from the proveo/hermes image: hermes' _get_cdp_override resolved the
' ws URL, Target.createTarget opened football.fantasysports.yahoo.com in the host
' Chrome, and `npx agent-browser@^0.26.0 --cdp` read that tab's URL back.
'
' ── HOST SIDE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   port    PROVEO_HOST_CDP_PORT, default 9222; Kit allow += localhost:<port>.
'   reuse   reuse a browser at the chosen port when /json/version advertises
'           a browser WebSocket. All harnesses reuse the same live endpoint
'           when their selected port matches it.
'           Chrome ≥136 refuses --remote-debugging-port on the default profile,
'           so a CDP-serving Chrome is never the everyday one.
'   launch  else Chrome/Chromium/Brave/Edge with --user-data-dir=
'           os.UserConfigDir()/proveo/host-chrome/<target>, in its own process
'           group, left open after the run so the login persists.
'   NOT ~/.proveo: that tree is mounted into sandboxes at /proveo-home, and the
'   profile's cookie store would be readable from the VM.
'
' ── WHAT THE AGENT CAN DO ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
' CDP is full control of that browser: every tab, every cookie in the profile.
' Page requests leave from host Chrome. The Kit's allow rule covers the CDP hop.
' The run warns so; the boundary is "log into only what the agent should touch".
' Since 2026-11-11 the browser opens before the sandbox,
' behind the live line "host-cdp — starting", which leaves the screen once CDP
' answers. ONE FACT PER ADD-ON (DECIDED 2026-11-11, the operator; the rejected
' alternatives: host-android-adb.puml): EnsureCDP
' returns hostdev.Opened{Browser, Profile}, and the interface block's Facts
' carry one row after `sbx create`:
'   ● chrome: Google Chrome · CDP 127.0.0.1:9333    profile ~/… dim under it
'   ● chrome: CDP 127.0.0.1:9333 (reused)           a browser already there
' then "⚠ host-cdp — the agent controls every tab and session in that browser".
' The reports ("host chrome: opened <bin> on profile <abs> …", "reusing the
' browser already serving CDP …") go to the run log alone (startAddon →
' ui.Logf), the profile absolute. Plain output draws no live line and writes
' "host-cdp — starting" to the run log only. --print reads "chrome: not
' started in print mode", CDP port and profile dim under it.
' Should sandbox.Run fail before its interface block, the fact and the items
' print anyway (Run's deferred flush; run.reportUnhanded before Run).
' [Unverified] whether sbx enforces the Kit allow on the direct (non-proxy) path;
' the host's global policy was allow-all during every measurement.

actor "Operator" as OP
node "host" as HOST {
  component "proveo run" as RUN
  component "Chrome\ndedicated profile\n127.0.0.1:<port>" as CH
}
node "sbx microVM" as VM {
  component "proveo-host-cdp\nguest discovery and WebSocket probe" as CDP
  component "agent-browser or Hermes\nrun-scoped CDP endpoint" as AG
}

OP --> CH : logs in once (2FA)
RUN --> CH : reuse or launch
RUN --> CDP : Kit allow localhost:<port>\nverify from the guest
CDP --> AG : supply the reachable endpoint
AG --> CH : CDP by IP, NO_PROXY

note right of CH
  **Dedicated, never everyday.** The profile
  lives outside ~/.proveo, so the VM cannot
  read its cookie store off the mount.
end note

note right of AG
  **Dial by IP.** Chrome rejects any Host
  that is not an IP or localhost, and builds
  its ws URL from that same Host.
end note
@enduml
